  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Obviously, the relation is not reflexive and transitive, but it is symmetric, because $x^{2}+x^{2}=2 x^{2} \\neq 1$\r\n\r\n$$\r\n\r\n\\begin{array}{l}\r\n\r\n\\text { and } x^{2}+y^{2}=1, y^{2}+z^{2}=1 \\\\\r\n\r\n\\Rightarrow x^{2}+z^{2}=1 \\\\\r\n\r\n\\text { But } x^{2}+y^{2}=1 \\Rightarrow y^{2}+x^{2}=1\r\n\r\n\\end{array}\r\n\r\n$$",
